received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Owner decision **D742 (A)** on #2729 ([comment](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/2729#issuecomment-7032920216)).\n\n**Change (1 file + release-note fragment):** `Session::on_task_finished` now emits the thread-idle lifecycle event once, right after the completed turn clears the active slot and *before* pending-work discovery, as rust-v0.167.0 does. The trailing emit after `maybe_start_turn_for_pending_work()` is removed, so a completed turn still reports idle exactly once (#2563's duplicate does not return).\n\n**D663 kept:** `maybe_start_turn_for_pending_work_with_sub_id` is unchanged: kill-switch early return (#445) → busy check → reserve → D171 refusal → capacity → discovery. While discovery is paused, Interrupt takes and marks the reserved turn; `pending_work_turn_configuration` then fails its `ptr_eq` check before `get_pending_input_for_task_start`, so the mail stays queued.\n\n**Accepted side effect (owner):** idle contributors (queued user input, goal continuation) now run before a mail-only wake reserves; the mail is then delivered as pending input in their turn.\n\nPrepared by sync-win2729b (`d742-prep.md`, patch (a)); implemented by sec-d742-747.\n\nFixes on sync (all platforms): `agent_message_wake::pending_agent_message_wake_respects_control_changes::{interrupt,kill_switch,plan_mode}_during_discovery`. Evidence (fail-before/pass-after on Linux, scratch `sync-ci/sec-d742` codex-core on Linux/macOS/Windows) follows in comments.\n\nKill-switch path: needs an Opus security review and a corbanu-security approval.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-20T07:10:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T09:50:29Z","closed_at":"2026-11-20T08:51:59Z","merged_at":"2026-11-20T08:51:59Z","merge_commit_sha":"81890da10ae347f558494f2dd77dcb632ad5b95d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"